Package: isa-check
Architecture: any
Depends: dpkg (>= 1.22.21ubuntu4), ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: list and probe compatible processor architecture variants
 isa-check reads dpkg's varianttable and checks every processor on the running
 system. With no arguments it lists all compatible variants in table order.
 With a variant argument it reports whether that variant is supported and
 returns a script-friendly status, including missing CPU features on failure.

Package: isa-preflight
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: verify CPU features or chain-load initramfs userspace
 isa-preflight is an executable intended to run as /init. When
 DEB_HOST_ARCH_VARIANT is set, it is freestanding and static, and checks every
 processor before any dynamic loader, shell, or init system runs. It reports
 missing CPU features, and halts on failure. Non-variant builds provide a
 dynamically linked no-op chainloader so image builders can use a uniform
 dependency and handoff.
 .
 Variant requirements are resolved from dpkg's varianttable at build time.
 On success the original init, moved to /next-init, is executed with the
 original arguments and environment. The included dracut module automatically
 installs isa-preflight as /init when the package is installed.
